claim.claim-text:
a graphics processor;
a central processing unit; and
a memory including a set of instructions, which when executed by one or more of the graphics processor or the central processing unit, cause the computing System to:

detect a first facial expression of a user;
detect a secondary input from the user that is associated with the first facial expression;
detect a focal point at a focus distance, wherein the focal point is associated with the user;
identify a depth of focus associated with the user based on a pupil dilation associated with the user;
determine a first size for the depth of focus based on the focus distance;
set a position of a focus area based on the focal point;
set a second size of the focus area based on the first size for the depth of focus; and
trigger an associated action based on the first facial expression, the secondary input and the focus area.

